# Dev Mode: Rules-Workflow Enhancement

## File Purpose and Relationship

This file defines the specific operation of the `dev-mode: rules-workflow @parameters/rules/dev-mode/dev-mode-rules-workflow-enhancement.mdc` message-command, which initializes developer mode with a focus on rules-workflow enhancement implementation from within rules-workflow. It should be consulted to understand:

- How to implement rules-workflow documentation enhancements
- Tool call sequences for analyzing rules-workflow code while modifying rules files
- Self-referential workflow boundary enforcement
- Verification strategies for rules-workflow enhancement documentation

This file complements:
- `fetch_rules(["knowledge/reference/guides/implementation-patterns"])`: Implementation continuation protocols
- `@parameters/rules/plan-mode/plan-mode-rules-workflow-enhancement.mdc`: Planning guidance for rules-workflow enhancements
- `@parameters/rules/dev-mode/continue-implementation-rules-workflow-enhancement.mdc`: Continuation guidance for rules-workflow enhancements
- `@parameters/rules/direct-mode/direct-mode-rules-workflow-enhancement.mdc`: Direct implementation approach without planning phase

## Usage as Project-Rule-Parameter

This file contains specialized implementation details for rules-workflow documentation enhancement. It should be referenced as a project-rule-parameter when initializing implementation for rules-workflow documentation enhancements:

```
dev-mode: rules-workflow @parameters/rules/dev-mode/dev-mode-rules-workflow-enhancement.mdc
```

For general implementation or other enhancement pathways, see the alternative project-rule-parameters listed in `@parameters/rules/README.mdc`.

## 1. Rules-Workflow Enhancement Implementation Overview

The rules-workflow enhancement implementation pathway provides a specialized execution structure optimized for enhancing rules-workflow documentation based on analysis of the actual rules-workflow code. This approach is ideal when:

- Documentation needs to reflect actual rules-workflow implementation patterns
- Self-referential knowledge needs to be captured
- Rules-workflow documentation needs to be created or updated
- Knowledge from rules-workflow codebase needs to be better organized within the cognitive architecture
- Rules-workflow patterns need to be standardized and documented for consistency

